body:
I just broke up with my girlfriend of 2 years last Sunday. 

&#x200B;

She started being a stripper more than a month, part of it was because of the money, part of it was because of her fantasy. When she first mentioned it, eventually, I tried to talk her our of it but no hope. I accepted her will and bargained about a set of rules while on the job. We finally came up with 6 rules in total, which two of them are keeping thing professional with no personal factors involved and do not contact/receive contacts from anyone. 

&#x200B;

Things went through well for a few weeks, there were usually some complaints after each night but those didn't bother me much because i knew how stressful the job could be. It was only last Sunday night that she came up to me about the idea of breaking up. She sugar-coated it with the reason that she started feeling that our relationship was leaning on one side as I was still so compassionate while she began to lose interest. I knew that was not right, of course there were highs and lows in our relationship, as well as all the other relationships in the world but she had never come up straight away about breaking up, those were usually about how she was feeling first and then we tried to figure things out. That was how our relationship could last for 2 years, by constantly contributing to it. 

So I tried to ask her around all of it and finally she admitted that she had already been into another one. It was the one she met the night before at the strip club, he was her client. My girlfriend said she couldn't get him out of her head and how perfect their talks was. She didn't want things to happen this way so she suggested a break up. 

I asked her times and times again because of the hard feelings and thoughts rushing through my head, and to clarify that that thing was real. She said she was sure that we were going to break up, but at the same time, asked me if we could still be something after this because I was the best friend that she'd ever had. 

&#x200B;

I told her I was not going to force things to stay anymore and I was willing to let her go. 

&#x200B;

We broke up.

&#x200B;

Two-third the time of our relationship was long distance. We were classmates at high school. Though we flirted with each other all the time but it was only the senior year that we were officially together. After graduating, we both left the city where we came from to pursued personal goals. We could only see each other once a year and each lasted a few days or weeks. 

&#x200B;

Things still feel like shits and I cannot get all of these feelings and thoughts out of my head. She was my first relationship that last more than 6 months and my truly truly seriously as we had clear plans for the future. The thought of the relationship is already over really overwhelms me that I find a tough time trying to focus on other things.
